From 962068a4080f9958d9dc4ea46f86fafadc830c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serghei Amelian <serghei.amelian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:17:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Skia] Sample scaled-down images from mipmaps

InterpolationQuality::Default (and Medium, High) map to bilinear (bicubic
for High) filtering without mipmaps.  Those filters read only the 2x2 (4x4)
source pixels nearest to each destination pixel, so an image drawn at less
than about half its size is point sampled: photos alias, screenshots shown
as thumbnails lose their text, a zone plate turns into moire.  The Cairo
port used CAIRO_FILTER_GOOD, which box-filters when scaling down.

Use trilinear filtering (SkMipmapMode::kLinear) when the image-to-device
matrix scales a raster image down in drawNativeImage() and drawPattern().
Low (live and animated resizes) and DoNotInterpolate are unchanged, as are
draws at 1:1 or scaled up and texture-backed images (Ganesh would copy them
into a new mipmapped texture, for every promise image again).  When painting
on the CPU, images whose mipmaps would not fit in half of Skia's resource
cache (32 MB) go without, so that they are not rebuilt for every tile.

Most draws are strict source rect draws (CSS backgrounds, border-image,
list markers; only RenderImage draws are not), and SkCanvas drops mipmaps
for those: the mipmaps of the whole image would mix in the pixels around
the source rect (the neighbouring sprites of a CSS sprite sheet).  So a
scaled-down strict draw whose source rect covers the whole image is drawn
as a fast one (there is nothing around it), and one of a part of the image
draws from a copy of that part with its own mipmaps.  The copies (at most
16 MB each) are kept in a small LRU cache (48 MB, 256 entries) keyed by the
source's unique ID, without keeping the source alive; a source drawn with
ever-changing, mostly overlapping parts (a fixed background while
scrolling) falls back to the strict draw without mipmaps after a few
changes instead of copying on every frame.  drawPattern() records its tile
(border-image slices, background-repeat: space/round) the same way.

Raster images sampled with mipmaps are not packed into the GPU image atlas
(its texture has no mipmaps, and mipmaps of an atlas would mix neighbouring
images), and the replay canvas does not substitute the atlas for such draws.

Measured with the Skia bundled in 2.54.3 (CPU raster and Ganesh GL),
downscaled against a Lanczos-3 reference (PSNR / SSIM):
  2048x2048 zone plate -> 280x280:   12.7 dB / 0.046  ->  30.7 dB / 0.769
  1920x1152 screenshot -> 400x240:   22.4 dB / 0.826  ->  34.4 dB / 0.975
  1920x1152 screenshot -> 640x384:   20.5 dB / 0.805  ->  32.6 dB / 0.973
and in WPE (GPU tiles, Mesa):
  <img> 1920x1152 -> 400x240:                22.4 dB  ->  32.8 dB
  background-size 400x240 / cover / contain: 22.4 dB  ->  32.8 dB
  background-repeat, 2048 -> 200 tiles:      12.8 dB  ->  35.7 dB
  background-repeat: space, same tiles:      13.0 dB  ->  34.9 dB
  border-image, 512px slices at 80px:        13.1 dB  ->  29.7 dB
  sprite (sheet 512 -> 128) 256 -> 64:       35.7 dB  ->  50.5 dB, no bleeding
